---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Studio — Greenbarn Creative Co."
  description="Greenbarn Creative Co. is a creative studio in Dearborn, Michigan, built on a decade of brand work."
  path="/studio"
  ogDescription="A decade of brand work, now under our own name."
>

<!-- ── HERO ── the barn -->
<header class="hero">
  <img src="/studio/barn.jpg" alt="The green barn the studio is named for">
  <div class="hero-title">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Studio</p>
      <h1>A studio, ten years<br>in the making.</h1>
    </div>
  </div>
</header>

<main>
  <div class="wrap">

    <!-- ── LEDE ── -->
    <section class="lede">
      <p>
        Greenbarn is a creative studio in Dearborn, Michigan. We make photography,
        film, and design for brands that would rather look like themselves than
        like everyone else.
      </p>
      <p>
        Most of what we know we learned somewhere else first. A decade of brand
        work across Bedrock, Cisco, the City of Detroit, and a long list of
        smaller shops taught us how a brand actually gets built and, more
        usefully, how it falls apart. We started Greenbarn to do that work
        directly, without the layers in between, and we scale the team to the
        job rather than the other way around.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- ── BIOS ── -->
    <section class="band">
      <div class="band-head">
        <p class="band-label">Who you work with</p>
      </div>

      <div class="bios">

        <div class="bio">
          <div class="portrait"><img src="/studio/evan.jpg" alt="Evan"></div>
          <h3>Evan </h3>
          <p class="role">Photo · Design · Web</p>
          <p>
            <!-- Draft. Rewrite in your own voice. -->
            Evan spent nearly eight years at Bedrock, finishing as Creative
            Director, then led the creative team for Cisco's global security
            brand. She covers photography, print, brand identity, and the web,
            along with the operations that keep a project on schedule.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="bio">
          <div class="portrait"><img src="/studio/justin.jpg" alt="Justin"></div>
          <h3>Justin</h3>
          <p class="role">Film · Motion</p>
          <p>
            <!-- Draft. Justin should write his own, or send you the details. -->
            Justin shoots and cuts. Brand films, event coverage, patient stories,
            and the kind of short work that has to hold attention in the first
            two seconds. He has been making video professionally for the better
            part of a decade, most of it alongside Evan.
          </p>
        </div>

      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ── CAPABILITIES ── -->
    <section class="band">
      <div class="band-head">
        <p class="band-label">What we do</p>
        <a class="band-link" href="/services">How to work with us &#8594;</a>
      </div>

      <div class="caps">
        <span>Photography</span>
        <span>Video and film</span>
        <span>Brand identity</span>
        <span>Art direction</span>
        <span>Creative direction</span>
        <span>Web design and build</span>
        <span>Print and packaging</span>
        <span>Event coverage</span>
        <span>Creative operations</span>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ── CLIENTS ── -->
    <section class="band">
      <div class="band-head">
        <p class="band-label">Selected clients</p>
      </div>
      <div class="clients">
        <span>Bedrock</span>
        <span>Cisco</span>
        <span>City of Detroit</span>
        <span>Crate &amp; Barrel</span>
        <span>Library Street Collective</span>
        <span>Downtown Detroit Partnership</span>
        <span>e3 Refillery</span>
        <span>Ilka Naumann, M.D.</span>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ── THE BARN ── -->
    <section class="band closer">
      <div>
        <h2>About<br><em>the barn.</em></h2>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p>
          <!-- Draft. This is the part worth writing yourself. -->
          Evan's parents had a green barn behind the house, and it was where
          everyone ended up. A whole crew of us, most days, building things and
          taking them apart, long before any of it counted as a career.
        </p>
        <p>
          Some of that crew still works together. The name came along because it
          was the most accurate thing we could think of, and because the studio
          runs the way the barn did. Whoever the work needs, in one room, making
          something.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

  </div>
</main>

</Layout>
